+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all (the initial call and 2 retries),
+with no pause between attempts. `ATTEMPTS` in `larder/capture.py` sets the limit. A successful attempt returns
+immediately; a third timeout is raised to the caller. Confirmation still waits for the gateway calls themselves.
+
+Previously, 5 attempts used growing pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds to spread calls across the gateway's Friday
+17:00–19:00 slowdown. That policy followed a Friday when 3 back-to-back attempts left 58 confirmed pantry orders
+for a volunteer to capture by hand; a sandbox replay with the spacing would have captured 57 of those 58.
+Three immediate attempts have been restored because members reported the extra 20 seconds of waiting on the
+confirmation page. This accepts the risk of more failed captures and manual follow-up during the slowdown.
+Switching gateways was ruled out because the contract runs to December 2026.
 
